>> title: Carne Asada
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: beef, mexican, grill, charcoal, tacos, marinade
>> counters: Taquería, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: asada, taco de asada, tacos de carne asada, carne asada tacos, grilled skirt steak, arrachera
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, guacamole, salsa-verde
>> servings: 6
>> time: 5 hr
>> slack: narrow — skirt is thin, so it goes from pink to grey while you fetch the plates; still a taco, just a chewy one

>> step: whisk the marinade
Whisk @fresh orange juice{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @fresh lime juice{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @soy sauce{2%Tbs}, @vegetable oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @garlic{6%cloves}(minced), @jalapeño{1}(seeded and minced), @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, @coarse black pepper{1%tsp}, and @cilantro{1/2%cup}(chopped, stems and all) together in a wide #dish{}.

>> step: marinate 4 hr, turning once
Marinate @outside skirt steak{2%lb}(900 g; trimmed of the membrane) in @&(~1)marinade{} for ~marinate{4%hr} in the fridge, turning it once.

>> step: grill 4 min a side, hard char
Grill @&(~1)marinated steak{} over a hot #charcoal grill{} ~grill{4%min} a side, salting it with @kosher salt{2%tsp} as it goes, until the outside is nearly black and the inside still pink.

>> step: rest 10 min
Rest @&(~1)grilled steak{} on the board for ~rest{10%min}, so the juice goes back into the meat rather than onto the knife.

>> step: chop across the grain, toss
Chop @&(~1)rested steak{} across the grain into small dice and toss it with @white onion{1/2%cup}(finely chopped) and @cilantro{1/2%cup}(chopped).
